fixup! Bug 2061218 - Save calendar event edits safely

Failure causes:
Two defects remain in the current event-save patch. CalModifyTransaction.doTransaction unconditionally awaits removePendingMoveCopies even when no recovery record exists. This postpones memory-calendar edits and redo notifications. Drag checks then see the old item, and task cleanup can use a stale generation. Affected jobs: 598898592, 598898559, 598898497, 598898522, 598898682, 598898601, 598898611, 598898610, 598898598, 598898692, 598898644, 598898502, 598898473, 598898482, 598898619. Separately, test_failedMoveCleanupCanRetryWithStorage intentionally retries additions after another editor changes the destination copy. CalStorageCalendar reports DUPLICATE_ID followed by MODIFICATION_FAILED. The registered calendar manager opens an error window, which crashes debug xpcshell because it has no WindowCreator. Affected jobs: 598898590, 598898544, 598898650, 598898637, 598898660, 598898558. All 49 jobs retain a settled assessment. Existing Nimbus failures affect 598898526, 598898608, 598898648, 598898484, 598898663, 598898539, 598898541, 598898657, 598898470, 598898653, 598898557. Job 598898571 contains existing Nimbus and crashreporter failures; 598898475 contains existing crashreporter failures. Existing accessibility and related UI failures affect 598898569, 598898627, 598898508, 598898513, 598898537, 598898639. Existing PDF selection failures affect 598898584, 598898505, 598898684, 598898486, 598898688, 598898493. Job 598898647 has the existing profile timestamp failure; 598898624 matches the quote-message timeout in bug 1894775. Job 598898560 is a worker shutdown followed by a completed retry. The old-title assertions in affected calendar jobs match bug 1897826, and the additional accessibility assertions in 598898592 have existing matches.

Changes:
calendar/base/src/CalTransactionManager.sys.mjs now awaits recovery only when pendingMoveCopies contains the source-item key. Ordinary modifications start immediately. Failed-move retries still await cleanup and retain the existing checks that preserve destination copies changed by another editor. calendar/test/unit/test_transaction_manager.js adds test_modifyMemoryItemsStartsBeforeYield. It checks immediate observer notifications for event and task commits and redo, then deletes the latest notified item. calendar cleanup and observer removal are registered. mail/components/calendar/test/unit/test_calendarEventEditSave.js captures provider error notifications only during the two expected preserved-copy retries. It preserves currentStatus, checks the exact DUPLICATE_ID and MODIFICATION_FAILED codes and duplicate-ID message, and restores normal error reporting in finally. Existing save-failure, copy-preservation, notification, Undo, and Redo assertions remain. No UI markup, labels, focus behavior, or accessibility checks changed. The relatedRepairs index and sourceUpdates list are empty, and priorFixup is null. No existing repair was duplicated or reused.

Validation:
AUTOCLOBBER=1 node artifacts/repair-validation/source-check.mjs passed. This focused source replay uses the actual transaction module, memory-provider modification and deletion methods, provider notification method, and checked-in regression/error-capture code with platform adapters. The regression failed on HEAD at the immediate observer assertion and passed with the repair for event and task commit/redo. Recovery checks passed for cleanup failure, later retry, missing copies, changed copies, and revised copies. Error-capture checks passed for exact errors, rejection of a wrong code, restoration of reporting, and forwarding of subsequent errors. Direct ESLint with the current comm configuration reported zero errors and warnings for all three changed files. Prettier --check passed for all three files. node --check passed for all three files. git diff --check passed. The final tracked diff contains only the three listed files; HEAD remains unchanged.

Validation limits:
Native xpcshell validation did not reach test execution. The direct runxpcshelltests.py harness selected test_transaction_manager.js from calendar/test/unit/xpcshell.toml, but the local macOS arm64 opt runtime exited with CrashReporter::OOPInit(): could not launch the crash helper and CrashReporter::SetExceptionHandler failed. A checkout-local application copy, explicit runtime paths, and adding its missing crashhelper did not resolve startup. The first harness attempt also hit EPERM while binding its HTTP helper and selected no tests; selection was corrected, and unused network helpers were omitted from later calendar-only attempts. ../mach commlint stopped during bootstrap because DNS access prevented downloading arrow==1.4.0; installed ESLint and Prettier were run directly instead. Native test_calendarEventEditSave.js, browser_dragEventItem.js, browser_taskUndoRedo.js, and browser_calendarEventEditSave.js remain unverified locally. The source replay is not a completed xpcshell or Thunderbird browser test. No build or clobber was required for these JavaScript changes. Fresh CI must confirm the repairs. Scratch scripts and logs are excluded from files.

